            "description": "Watch Belgium vs Iran highlights and goals from World Cup 2026 on ReFooty: Football Highlights Hub. Match played on June 22, 2026. Two tactical setups collided on a high-stakes night in the World Cup, where every inch of the pitch was fought for with immense intensity. The encounter promised drama from the first whistle, with both nations desperate to claim an advantage in the group standings. Early VAR Drama and Goalkeeping Heroics On June 22, 2026 , Belgium and IR Iran faced off in a World Cup clash defined by fine margins and missed opportunities. The physical nature of the game was established early when Romelu Lukaku received a yellow card just three minutes in. Belgium dominated possession and created several openings through Kevin De Bruyne , but found Alireza Beiranvand in sensational form. The most pivotal moment of the first half arrived in the 25th minute; Mehdi Taremi thought he had put Iran ahead, but after a tense VAR review, the goal was overturned. Thibaut Courtois was equally sharp at the other end, producing a brilliant save to deny Hossein Kanani 's goalbound effort. Second Half Tension and a Costly Red Card The second period saw Belgium ramp up the pressure, with Maxim De Cuyper and Dodi Lukébakio forcing more saves from the inspired Beiranvand . However, the momentum shifted dramatically in the 66th minute when Nathan Ngoy was shown a straight red card. Reduced to ten men, Belgium had to recalibrate their approach while resisting a revitalized Iranian side. Mehdi Taremi continued to be a threat, forcing another save from Courtois as the match moved into its final stages. A Frantic Finish Under the Lights Despite the man disadvantage, Belgium pushed for a late winner. Hans Vanaken and Youri Tielemans orchestrated attacks that kept the Iranian defense on high alert. In the dying moments of stoppage time, Dodi Lukébakio had a final chance to steal the victory, but his left-footed strike curled agonizingly wide of the post. The match concluded in a 0-0 stalemate, leaving Belgium to rue their finishing while IR Iran celebrated a hard-earned point built on a foundation of defensive discipline and goalkeeping excellence.",
